<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William, Prince of Albania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1876">1876</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Wilhelm of Wied, Prince Wilhelm of Wied</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William, Prince of Albania, born Prince Wilhelm of Wied, was a German officer chosen by the Great Powers in 1913 as ruler of the new Principality of Albania. He arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> in March 1914 but faced rebellion in central Albania, rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essad-pasha-toptani">Essad Pasha Toptani</a> and the outbreak of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and left the country in September 1914 after six months, without formally abdicating.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-prince-of-albania.jpg" alt="William, Prince of Albania" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Princ_Vidi_(portret).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
